ason: T8 is part of a possible chow with T7 and T9, but since T7 has already been played, the chow is unlikely to be completed. Discarding T8 avoids giving others a chance to form a meld, while retaining pairs and other tiles for potential high-value patterns like pungs or Seven Pairs.\nAnswer: Play T8"}
